      "side": 1,
      "message": "Quickly checking online, it looks like `getifaddrs()` is expected to return an entry even for an interface with no address. This is basically kernel dependent. Following on our sync this morning, this is probably a detail we might want to check with CTS or with a (real) integration test.\n\nIt will also probably be hard to have a legitimate interface without at least an IPv6 link local address.\n\n\u003e /sys/class/net which generally seems like the better approach (though I am not sure system server has access to that directory)\n\nCurious just in general outside of the context of this particular patch: can we officially depend on sysfs in the system server ?",
